 # Crash recovery
 
+**2026-10-20 independent retention check (`cd8861c`):** The original P32 heartbeat-ownership and repair-log privacy failures still pass the native/synthetic reproductions, along with the affected recovery suites. This confirms those fixes within tested scope; full live recovery, optional-worker/circuit-breaking gates and universal redaction remain unverified. The isolated launcher reports `repair_required`. Prompt 33 remains blocked by a separate account identity finding. [Current reconciliation](../artifacts/jarvis-audit/modules/33-mcp-integrations/2026-10-19-independent-cd8861c/codex-findings-reconciliation.md).
+
 Jarvis on Windows uses a virtual environment redirector which can have a different
 PID from the actual Python interpreter. Checking its heartbeat against the
 redirector PID caused false startup timeouts and repeated restarts.
